    "result_text": "All 284 tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented audit logging for successful owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (which handles the `POST /api/owners` endpoint).\n\nChanges:\n- Added a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`: `LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\")`.\n- In `addOwner`, immediately after `saveOwner` succeeds, log the authenticated user, the new owner's id, and the membership number:\n  ```java\n  AUDIT.info(\"Owner created by user={} ownerId={} membershipNumber={}\",\n      currentUsername(), owner.getId(), owner.getMembershipNumber());\n  ```\n- Added a `currentUsername()` helper that reads the authenticated principal from `SecurityContextHolder`, falling back to `\"anonymous\"` when there's no authentication.\n\nThe log line is emitted only on the success path (after the save), so failed creations are not recorded. The new `Cp19Tests` acceptance test and the full suite (284 tests) are green.",
